{{draft}} {{infobox shinto shrine | religious_affiliation = Shinto | image = Nitta-shrine (satsuma-sendai) pavilions 1.jpg | consecration_year = 1358 | type = [[Sōja (Shinto)|Sōja shrine]] | deity = [[Hachiman]] [[Susanoo]] ([[Gozu Tenno]]) [[Nitta Yoshisada]] all the deities of its province ([[Sōja (Shinto)|Sōja shrine]]) }} {{ill|Nitta Shrine (Satsumasendai City)|lt=Nitta Shrine|simple|Nitta Shrine|4=ja|5=新田神社 (薩摩川内市)}} is a [[Shinto shrine]] located in [[Japan]]. It is a shrine of the [[Goryo]] faith.<ref name=":0" /> The Nitta Shrine houses both the Nitta Hachimangu, an [[ichinomiya]], and the Shukō Jinja, a [[Sōja shrine]].
It contains Nitta Hachimangu, an [[ichinomiya]], but itself is larger than merely that
== {{Anchor|Hachimangu}}Hachimangu == Nitta Hachimangu is a [[Hachiman shrine]] located within this shrine
== {{Anchor|Shukō Jinja}}Shukō Jinja == {{nihongo|Shukō Jinja|九楼守公神社}} is a [[Sōja (Shinto)|Sōja shrine]]. It enshrines all the [[kami]] of the shrines in [[Satsuma Province|Satsuma]] [[Provinces of Japan|Province]].
It is a subshrine of Nitta Shrine
== See Also ==
* [[Ichinomiya]] * [[Hirasaki Shrine|Hirakiki jinja]] (the other Ichinomiya of [[Satsuma Province]]) * {{ill|Nitta Shrine (Ōta City)|ja|新田神社_(大田区)}}
